{
  "title": "Cold-shoe mount with GoPro prongs (for the Insta360 GO Ultra in a printed frame)",
  "summary": "Slides into any cold or hot shoe (camera, rig, light stand) and ends in three GoPro-style prongs. The GO Ultra in its Action Pod goes in a printed protective frame with two prongs, so the flip screen stays usable. A knurled wheel clamps the foot in the shoe.",
  "status": "preview",
  "date": "2026-11-26",
  "material": "PLA (printed hardware settings: 0.12 mm layers, 6 walls, 60 % gyroid)",
  "notes": "All printed, nothing bought. Foot: ISO-style shoe foot, 1.9 mm thick, in two widths on the plate (one rear notch = 18.20 mm, two notches = 18.45 mm): keep the one that slides into the shoe snug and recycle the other. The foot carries a printed M11 x 1.5 stud; the knurled wheel screws down onto the shoe's lips and clamps the foot (works for lips 0.5 to 2.6 mm thick). The plastic foot has no metal, so it can't short a hot shoe's contacts. Head: same three GoPro prongs, M5 thumbscrew and M5 nut pocket as the Kinect rig's phone riser. The camera side is a separately printed protective frame for the GO Ultra + Action Pod with two GoPro prongs (a MakerWorld model under the Standard Digital File License, printed for personal use and not shown here); its prongs go between these three. The head presses onto a square key on the stud (4 directions); put the wheel on first, then the head, and add a drop of CA glue if it should never come off. Plate for TNT: white PLA at 230 C, flow cap 12 mm3/s, 1 h 18 min, 16 g, no supports, no brim. The thumbscrew is the tallest part, so its last ~5 mm print alone; it is the same thumbscrew that printed fine on the rig's knob plate.",
